ENCODER PULL-UPS (required)

All four resistors join at 3.3V. Each free end goes to its own pin only:

                 ┌─ 4.7k ─→ GPIO36
3.3V (Pin 1) ────┼─ 4.7k ─→ GPIO39
                 ├─ 4.7k ─→ GPIO34
                 └─ 4.7k ─→ GPIO35
5 ToF SENSORS

All five share these four connections:

VIN → 5V
GND → GND
SDA → GPIO21
SCL → GPIO22

Each one gets its own XSHUT pin and I2C address:

Left         XSHUT → GPIO23   address 0x30
Left-front   XSHUT → GPIO19   address 0x31
Front        XSHUT → GPIO18   address 0x32
Right-front  XSHUT → GPIO17   address 0x33
Right        XSHUT → GPIO16   address 0x34
MPU6050
VCC → 5V
GND → GND
SDA → GPIO21
SCL → GPIO22
AD0 → GND (address 0x68)
INT, XDA, XCL → not connected
BUTTONS
Button 1 : GPIO4  → button → GND   (INPUT_PULLUP)
Button 2 : GPIO13 → button → GND   (INPUT_PULLUP)
POWER
Battery +    → TB6612 VM
Battery +    → buck converter IN+
Buck OUT 5V  → ESP32 pin 19 (5V), ToF VIN, MPU VCC, encoder VCC
Battery −    → common GND

Connect all of these grounds together: battery, buck, ESP32, TB6612, encoders, ToF sensors and MPU6050.

RESISTORS
Encoders: four 4.7k resistors, required.
I2C: no resistors, because the sensor modules have their own pull-ups. Add 4.7k to 3.3V on SDA and SCL only if the bus doesn't work.
Buttons: no resistors, because INPUT_PULLUP handles them.
WIRE GAUGE
Battery, VM, buck input, main GND  → 22 AWG
Motor wires                        → 26 AWG
All signals and sensor power       → 28–30 AWG
