CHECK BEFORE PLUGGING IN THE ESP32
Buck output: it should read 5.0V.
SDA/SCL: both must read 3.3V or less, never 5V.
Encoder C1/C2: turn the wheel by hand. Each signal must switch between 0V and about 3.3V, never 5V.
In code: turn on the PCNT glitch filter for all four encoder pins.
